summary: Provision a FreeIPA env and run its job recipe
description: |
    This test lives in the separate ci-freeipa repository; the plan in the
    FreeIPA repo under test discovers it from this repo at a pinned ref.
    Runs on a Testing Farm guest (or locally). When KOJI_TASK_ID is set
    (Fedora dist-git CI: Packit already ran a Koji scratch build for the
    PR) the test REUSES that build -- it downloads the task's RPMs and
    bakes the channel images from them, with no SRPM and no build image.
    Otherwise the plan's prepare step installs the BuildRequires of
    freeipa.spec.in, so when no SRPM URL is supplied the test builds
    freeipa's SRPM directly on the guest: from a clone of FREEIPA_REPO_URL
    at FREEIPA_REPO_REF, from the dist-git tree the plan ships
    (FREEIPA_DISTGIT), or from the checkout given in FREEIPA_SRC (local
    runs). It bakes the batch's channel images ONCE, then runs every
    preset in the batch (FREEIPA_JOBS) through the same freeipa-env
    up/run/down flow a local or ssh queue job would, reusing the packages
    and channel images across presets. Exits with the worst per-job run
    status.
test: bash ./tf-runner.sh
duration: 12h
result: custom
